* UPGRADE_MASTERS
* S.67 stage 1 (owner, 17 Oct 2026).  Set up the master files and copy every registered account's VOC and dictionaries into them.
*
* voc_master, dict_master and master_state live in the SDSYS account and hold a copy of every account's VOC records and dictionary records.  They are
* kept in step afterwards by the file-change hook and the journal, so this only has to make the first copy, and again after an upgrade: UPDATE.ACCOUNTS
* has just rewritten the VOC records of every kept account, and a RESTORE or an old system's files reached the accounts without the hook.
*
* It is NOT a one-time walk: it makes the master copies equal to the accounts' every time it is run, which changes nothing that is already right.  An
* edit made directly to a master record is therefore replaced by the account's record, which is stage 1's rule (the account is the truth).
*
* RUN gpl.bp upgrade_masters       set the master files up and copy every account into them
*
* It runs from the installer, as sd -internal and root, after the accounts have been brought forward and before the register is handed to sdsys, and it
* prints COMPLETE on a line of its own when, and only when, every account was copied with no error.  The installer matches on that word and nothing
* else.  A run that did not reach it is reported and the install goes on: nothing else depends on the master files, and the next install (or SYNC.MASTERS
* at a terminal, as SDSYS) does it again.
*
* START-HISTORY:
* 19 Oct 26 dm  The verifier's finding F7: ONE kernel call for every account ('syncall') in place of one for each, each of which read the whole of every master file
*               (a full sync of 400 accounts took over a minute and a half, and the installer runs one on every install).
* 19 Oct 26 dm  New.
* END-HISTORY
*
* START-CODE

$internal
program upgrade_masters

$include syscom keys.h
$include int$keys.h

   rep = ''
   ans = ''
   s0 = 0
   account = ''
   rowv = ''
   failed = 0
   copied = 0
   i = 0

   call !masters_setup(rep)
   if rep<1> # 0 then
      crt 'The master files could not be set up: ' : rep<2>
      stop
   end
   crt 'Master files: ' : rep<2>

   ans = kernel(K$MASTERS, 'syncbegin')
   if ans<1> # 0 then
      crt 'The master files cannot be used (status ' : ans<1> : ').'
      stop
   end
   s0 = ans<2>
*  Every account in one call; one field for each, its name and then the seven numbers 'sync' gives, as values.
   ans = kernel(K$MASTERS, 'syncall')
   if ans<1> # 0 then
      crt 'The accounts could not be copied (status ' : ans<1> : ').'
      stop
   end
   for i = 2 to dcount(ans, @fm)
      rowv = ans<i>
      account = rowv<1, 1>
      copied += 1
      if rowv<1, 8> > 0 then
         failed += 1
         crt 'Account ' : account : ': ' : rowv<1, 8> : ' error(s) while copying'
      end
   next i
   rep = kernel(K$MASTERS, 'syncend' : @fm : s0)

   crt 'Master files: ' : copied : ' account(s) copied, ' : failed : ' with errors'
   if failed = 0 then crt 'COMPLETE'
   stop

end

* END-CODE
